{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE CLOSE WAS WRONG, AND THE FIX FOR THE BEDROCK BUG IS WHAT PROVED IT\n\nThe operator reopened this epic on the rule that closing without completion verification is prohibited. Debugging the Bedrock error showed that ruling was right for a reason nobody had yet seen: **the verification that produced the earlier PASS was blind.**\n\nSame command, same ticket, same instance — only the max_tokens clamp differs ([rebar:1019-e1e9-5117-4795], Gerrit 1361):\n\n    BEFORE   128 provider 400s, 32 of 32 epic-bug-screen calls FAILED   ->  verdict PASS\n    AFTER      0 provider 400s,  0 screen failures                      ->  verdict FAIL (exit 1)\n\nEvery screen call was hitting a Bedrock 400 (a cap raised for the 128K verifier riding into the 64K trivial model), and `epic_bug_screen._row` degrades a failed screen to **C — 'unrelated'**. So the caused_by bug floor evaluated NOTHING and reported no findings. The PASS was an artifact of a blind gate.\n\n### What the verifier says once it can actually see\n\nTwo findings, both legitimate:\n\n 1. **AC4, the `[operator-attested]` criterion** — 'requires a concrete attestation with verifiable specifics'; the comments cite a run against an OLD sha (96b82de1e0). This is INDEPENDENTLY the same gap my own read-only verification pass flagged: the epic carries a `plan-review` attestation and no completion/operator attestation, so the tag rests on narrative comments. Two independent checks, same conclusion. **I have unticked AC4** — it is not honestly met.\n 2. **Open bug [rebar:2e47-ae62-c0cf-48a0] indicts this epic's subtree** — rebar's hardcoded Jira vocabularies disagree with a real DC instance (`LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA['idea']='IDEA'` does not exist on DC; label limit is 254 not 255; duplicate Task type). That bug is the capability map's own output, filed during this epic and still open.\n\nFinding 2 is the epic-bug-screen doing precisely its job, for the first time. It was invisible for as long as the screen was blind.\n\n### So the epic is correctly OPEN\n\nIt should not close until AC4 has a real attestation and 2e47 is resolved or explicitly dispositioned. Recording plainly that the earlier close was not merely missing a signature — the underlying verdict was wrong, and it was wrong in the permissive direction."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858390442022001,"uuid":"c1d3c2a1-03fa-4fe3-80b5-0d2e3284c6ed"}